The dictionary at internal/words/english.txt is built from the Automatically
Generated Inflection Database (AGID), version 2016.01.19, obtained from
https://wordlist.aspell.net. Nothing of it appears in code forge generates: it
is read by the generator and never shipped to a user's program.

What forge keeps of it is a small part of the whole — noun singular and plural
pairs the regular rules do not already reach, a vocabulary of singular nouns
ending in s, and the verbs whose final consonant doubles. The notices below are
reproduced in full all the same, because that is what each of them asks for.

